        <!-- Section 3: What is Moissanite? (Verbatim copy from media_1787461024030.md) -->
        <div class="comp-info-block">
            <div class="comp-info-text">
                <h2 class="comp-info-title">What is Moissanite?</h2>
                <p class="comp-body-para">Moissanite is a high-brilliance, silicon-carbide gemstone originally discovered in a meteorite impact site by scientist Dr. Henri Moissan in 1893. Due to its intense fire and incredible strength, it was initially mistaken for natural diamond. Since naturally occurring space moissanite is extremely rare on Earth, all gem-quality moissanite today is cultivated in advanced, eco-controlled laboratory environments.</p>
                <p class="comp-body-para">Renowned for outshining almost every other gem, moissanite possesses a higher refractive index than diamond, giving it exceptional brilliance and rainbow light dispersion. With a score of 9.25 to 9.50 on the Mohs hardness scale, it stands as one of the hardest minerals on earth—second only to diamond. At Sat Jewels, our precision-crafted lab moissanites offer fine jewelry lovers a sustainable, 100% ethical, and budget-smart alternative without ever compromising on beauty or lifetime durability.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="comp-info-img-wrap">
                <img src="/assets/ivevar/Moissanite_Halo_Ring_800x800.jpg" alt="What is Moissanite Gemstone" class="comp-info-img" />
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 4: What is Lab Grown Diamond? (Verbatim copy from media_1787461024030.md) -->
