            <div class="comp-info-img-wrap">
                <img src="/assets/ivevar/Moissanite_Solitaire_Ring_800x800.jpg" alt="What is Lab Grown Diamond" class="comp-info-img" />
            </div>
            <div class="comp-info-text">
                <h2 class="comp-info-title">What is a Lab-Grown Diamond?</h2>
                <p class="comp-body-para">A lab-grown diamond is an authentic diamond cultivated above ground using state-of-the-art technological methods such as Chemical Vapor Deposition (CVD) or High Pressure High Temperature (HPHT). These innovative processes precisely replicate the natural thermal and geological conditions under which mined diamonds form in the earth's mantle.</p>
                <p class="comp-body-para">As a result, lab-created diamonds share the exact chemical structure, physical hardness (10/10 on the Mohs scale), and optical brilliance of earth-mined diamonds—making them virtually identical even to certified gemologists. At Sat Jewels, our lab-grown diamonds provide a 100% conflict-free, eco-conscious, and financially smart luxury option, allowing you to enjoy the timeless elegance of a real diamond without the heavy environmental or financial impact of traditional diamond mining.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 5: What is Diamond? (Verbatim copy from media_1787461024030.md) -->
        <div class="comp-info-block">
            <div class="comp-info-text">
                <h2 class="comp-info-title">What is a Natural Diamond and why are conscious buyers shifting toward ethical alternatives?</h2>
                <p class="comp-body-para">Natural diamonds are pure carbon minerals formed over millions of years under intense heat and pressure deep within the Earth's mantle. Renowned for their timeless prestige and maximum hardness (10/10 on the Mohs scale), they have long been a traditional choice for fine jewelry.</p>
                <p class="comp-body-para">However, traditional earth-mining processes often carry significant environmental consequences, including soil erosion, habitat destruction, and heavy carbon emissions. Furthermore, the historic mined-diamond trade has been linked to conflict gems that fund regional instability and unethical labor practices.</p>
                <p class="comp-body-para">At Sat Jewels, we respect the legacy of fine gemstones while prioritizing the future of our planet. That is why we specialize in 100% ethical, conflict-free, and sustainable jewelry solutions that deliver identical luxury without the environmental footprint.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="comp-info-img-wrap">
